    <h2>Project Overview</h2>

    <p>
        Traditional composite resin-infusion tooling is typically designed
        around a specific part geometry. This means that new tooling often
        needs to be manufactured for every new part, requiring additional
        material, manufacturing time, and workspace.
    </p>

    <p>
        The goal of this project was to develop a standardized resin-infusion
        table that separates the reusable vacuum-sealing surface from the
        part-specific mold. Smaller interchangeable molds can then be installed
        into the table rather than manufacturing an entirely new infusion tool
        for every part.
    </p>

    <p>
        The system was also designed as an educational platform that could be
        used to demonstrate composite resin-infusion technology to students.
    </p>


