<section>

    <h2>Design Concept</h2>

    <p>
        The primary design concept was to separate the vacuum-sealing
        flange from the actual part mold.
    </p>

    <p>
        Rather than creating a complete infusion tool for every new
        geometry, the table provides the reusable sealing surface while
        a smaller thermoformed insert contains the geometry of the part.
    </p>


    <div class="highlight">

        <strong>Key Design Feature:</strong>

        <p>
            A 6-inch flange surrounding the mold cavity provides the
            required area for the vacuum seal. By integrating this flange
            into the reusable table, only the smaller mold insert needs
            to change between parts.
        </p>

    </div>


